course: dictionary
lesson: 4855
title: Hypo: a short word with a big meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Context, the words around a word, gives you clues. «I'm having a hypo» is short for hypoglycaemia, which means blood sugar that has fallen too low. Hypo is an informal word, so you will often hear it from friends or family.
explain: «A hypo is blood sugar too low, from too much insulin, too little food or extra exercise; signs are shaking, sweating, paleness, crossness or confusion.» Look at the signs in the list. They all describe a body that is unwell, so a hypo is a health problem, not a sound or an animal. Try swapping in your meaning: "A hypo is sugar that is too low" still makes sense.
explain: The prefix «hypo-» means under or below. Hypothermia starts the same way, and it means the body is too cold, below its normal temperature. When you spot a prefix, you can often guess the rest of the word.
fact: Hypo is short for hypoglycaemia, when the sugar in the blood is too low.
fact: «Too little sugar is a hypo: shaky, pale, sweaty, cross or confused.»
fact: «A hypo is treated with fast sugar such as glucose tablets or juice, then the level is checked again in 15 minutes.»
fact: If someone has a hypo, tell an adult straight away.
fact: Informally, hypo can also short for a hypodermic needle, which is a syringe.
exercise: «Too little sugar is a hypo: shaky, pale, sweaty, cross or confused.» Which of these is a sign of a hypo? | *Shaky | Full of energy and bouncing | Sunburnt | Singing loudly
exercise: Your friend says, «I'm having a hypo.» What should they have straight away? | A long run around the park | *Juice or glucose tablets | A cold bath | Nothing, wait until dinner
exercise: In «hypothermia», the prefix «hypo-» means? | Very fast | Inside out | *Under or below | Over or above
test: «A hypo is treated with fast sugar such as glucose tablets or juice.» What treats a hypo? | Hot soup and a long sleep | *Fast sugar, such as juice | Waiting for it to pass without eating | Cold water on the face
test: In «hypothermia», the prefix «hypo-» means below, so what is the body like? | Too noisy | *Too cold | Too tall | Too hot
exam: Which is the best meaning of «a hypo» in «I'm having a hypo»? | A kind of dance | A very large bowl of soup | Blood sugar has fallen too low | *A short, informal word for blood sugar too low
